+We have added a source-to-target result and state equivalence study in Section~IV (Evaluation). On 100 randomly sampled MySQL test cases transferred to DuckDB, \tool{} achieves 52.0\% result equivalence and 74.0\% state equivalence, compared with 14.0\%/56.0\% for SQLGlot, 34.0\%/65.0\% for RISE, and 38.0\%/69.0\% for \sedar{}. Details can be found in \metareviewref{1}. We have also renamed ``Semantic Correctness'' to ``Execution Validity'' throughout the paper and clarified its definition in Section~IV (Evaluation) to distinguish runtime executability from result or state equivalence.
 
